  "body": "fix(worker): stop the systemic ~2s worker fast-exit (52/70 failed rows)\n\nRCA (task-20260815-215959-rca-and-resume--gtm-certification-worker):\nUMR-20260815-033344-4799 died 05:12:10 to 05:12:12 (2.3s). Real cause,\nfrom task.yaml's own checkpoint note: preflight-guard.py's\ntight_task_schema_violation hard stop fired because prompt.txt's\nCOMPLEXITY_TIER was \"moderate\", not a member of tight_task_validation.\nVALID_TIERS. pm_lifecycle.py build_tightened_prompt() defaulted (and 2\ncall sites plus the CLI arg) complexity_tier=\"moderate\". Fixed to\n\"integrative\" at all 4 sites, and build_tightened_prompt() now\nvalidates its own assembled prompt against the same real gate before\never dispatching, so this class of bug fails loud and immediate\ninstead of silently burning a real dispatch and worker unit lifecycle.\n\nAlso: mark-umr-terminal gains --logs-ref, and worker-exit-status-\nbridge.py now passes the task's own worker.log path on every failed\nwrite, so umr_tasks.logs_ref stops being permanently NULL.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
